  "rewrites": {
   "7": {
    "original": "Communities Blessed will begin at 6 p.m. at the Bowen Ingram Stadium with music from the King University Acappella Band, live music from the Miine Britt is Friends, comedy from Anthony Brown and performances by the King University Bison.",
    "rewrite": "The celebration in Communities Blessed starts at 6 p.m. at the Bowen Ingram Stadium featuring music by the King University Acappella Band, live performances from Miine Britt is Friends, humor from Anthony Brown, and acts by the King University Bison."
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "Unity in Health is a community-based health education center that aims to improve outcomes by addressing the social determinants of health.",
    "rewrite": "Unity in Health is a community-centered health education hub focused on enhancing results through the mitigation of social determinants of health."
   },
   "13": {
    "original": "The picnic spot includes shells with food, drinks and a live band and plastic cut, which can be brought up to the concert.",
    "rewrite": "The picnic area features shells for eating and drinking, a live band, and plastic utensils, which can be brought to the event."
   },
   "9": {
    "original": "If they bring canned goods to the event, prices drop to $10 for adults, $5 for kids and a stuffed animal.",
    "rewrite": "If canned goods are brought to the event, then adults' prices drop to $10, kids' prices to $5, and include a stuffed animal."
   },
   "11": {
    "original": "Picnic areas will open at 7 p.m., including the one on Frey Avenue across from the stadium.",
    "rewrite": "Picnic areas, such as the one on Frey Avenue opposite the stadium, will become available at 7 p.m."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "Tickets for the concert are $14 for adults and $5 for kids 8 and under.",
    "rewrite": "The concert ticket price is $14 for adults and $5 for children 8 years old and younger."
   },
   "12": {
    "original": "Tickets for the picnic are $5.",
    "rewrite": "Prices for the picnic tickets are $5 each."
   },
   "10": {
    "original": "All proceeds will go to the hospitals.",
    "rewrite": "All proceeds will benefit the hospitals."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "are trying to get as many people as possible to donate to Unity in Sickness and Unity in Health, two health care foundations at nearby hospitals. Unity in Health is a community-centered health education hub focused on enhancing results through the mitigation of social determinants of health.\n\"This is a positive way to have students and community members engaged in football while also being involved in helping the community in a positive way,\" Burroughs said.\nJust ask Sykes.\n\"At least on this trip visiting North Canton, I asked (Burroughs) my question first, about Unity in the Community, which is great, and I know it\u2019s just the beginning,\" Sykes said after returning from the trip to the Buffalo area.\n\u201cIt\u2019s just to keep everybody involved in the community and keep everybody helping people in the community. We all have moms, dads, granddads, uncles, brothers, sisters, friends that potentially can be hurt, get sick or married so hopefully right in our three or four years in college that we kind of understand how what we can do and help and what we can do with our music, whatever type of humor we can do, whatever our talent may be it\u2019s just to get involved in the community and bless the community.\u201d\nThe celebration in Communities Blessed starts at 6 p.m. at the Bowen Ingram Stadium featuring music by the King University Acappella Band, live performances from Miine Britt is Friends, humor from Anthony Brown, and acts by the King University Bison.\nThe concert ticket price is $14 for adults and $5 for children 8 years old and younger. If canned goods are brought to the event, then adults' prices drop to $10, kids' prices to $5, and include a stuffed animal. All proceeds will benefit the hospitals.\nPicnic areas, such as the one on Frey Avenue opposite the stadium, will become available at 7 p.m. Prices for the picnic tickets are $5 each. The picnic area features shells for eating and drinking, a live band, and plastic utensils, which can be brought to the event.\nAnd Burroughs made sure King fans don't forget about Uncle Rico Film's football comedy \u2014 named for the character Sean William",
